      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-05_WidnesExaminer_art0017" n="art0017">
        <head>TREATMENT OF PHTHISTS.</head>
        <p>TREATMENT OF PHTHISTS.</p>
        <p>It was resolved by the Health Committee that the committee take a few hopeful cases of phthisis into the hospital at Aikin-street for treatment. Councillor Evatis, in moving the adoption of the minutes, explained that Aikin-street hospital had not many patients at present, and they proposed to send there three or four cases of phthisis as an experiment. A large number of persons in the town wore affected with phthisis, and the disease was now recognized to be a source of danger. The cases would be those of people who were unable to help themselves. Councillor BuitTox seconded, and the minutes were passed.</p>
      </div>
