        <head>i tree, I called: ..... LADY DAFFODIL. ",;.'3,.... mpumMill.....* I3Y MARI'. F. I,IIARPE: , WhOO rs ~ „.?4,',...,,,,t4-4,1 _</head>
        <p>i tree, I called: ..... LADY DAFFODIL. ",;.'3,.... mpumMill.....* I3Y MARI'. F. I,IIARPE: , WhOO rs ~ „.?4,',...,,,,t4-4,1 _</p>
        <p>My dainty Lady Daffodil Has donned her amber gown, And on her fair and sunny head 6parkles her golden crown. The conscious bluebell e softly sway, And catch the yellow light— And violets, among their leaves, Breathe low their young delight. The sweet old-fashioned aluaOnd flower 'Brightens its, pallid red, And flings its petals, daintily, Ct Over the garden bed. Her tall green leaves, like sentinel', Surround my Lady's throne, And graciously in happy state She reigns a queen alone. And thus, my Lady Daffodil In gorgeous amber gown, Holdeth her court this sun-warm day, Wearing her golden crown.</p>
