      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-05_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>Undisturbed Inner Tubes.</head>
        <p>Undisturbed Inner Tubes.</p>
        <p>Cases come under notice from time to time of riders who have used roadster tyres for two or three seasons without once having had occasion to remove their tyres for the purpose of repairing a puncture. Something akin to exultation is naturally experienced by these lucky cyclists, until the fatal day arrives when an investigation has to be made. Then it frequently happens that the air-tube is found to be firmly stuck to the inside of the cover, and, unless considerable patience and caution are exercised in separating one from the other, a rent is likely to be made, giving some trouble to repair. For this reason it is well worth while to examine the tubes, say, once a year, in a leisurely manner. If the inner lining of the cover be well dusted with 'french chalk, the liability of sticking will be reduced to the minimum.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-05_WidnesExaminer_art0087" n="art0087">
        <head>Selecting a Frame Size.</head>
        <p>Selecting a Frame Size.</p>
        <p>The inexperienced cyclist is apt to be seized with an ambition to ride a higher sized frame than is necessary, forgetful of the fact that the ad- ditional weight tells against him. A suitable size of frame is arrived at by measuring the length of leg from fork to heel, and deducting the length of crank' and another two or three inches for the saddle. Any doubt should be settled by ordering the next size below that indicated by the net measurement, as there is no objection to exposing an inch or two of saddle pillar, as required. Whe- ther a backward or forward position be adopted as regards the saddle, the leg should never be stretched to its full extent at any point in the pedal's revolu- tion. Even a frame too small is preferable to one too larv:e.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-05-05_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <p>GREAT SANKEY AFFAIRS.</p>
