        <p>Ales K. Jrd, -dives an.. Mr. W. J. Ford, timepiece Mr. G. Ford and Miss Ellison, curb Mr. and Mrs. F. Ford, toilet service Miss E. Mounfleld, ornaments and cushion Mr. C. Mounfleld, overmantel, Mr. H. Mounfleld, chair Mr. and Mrs. J. Mounfleld, coal cabinet Miss Fairhurst, cushion Mr. W. Scotson and Miss E. Lewis, tea service Mr. and Miss Heath, fish knives and forks Messrs. Crestleld and Sons, Limited, Staff, time-piece Miss L. Whittaker, silver butter knife Mrs. Broadhurst, glass preserve jar Mr. E. C. Jones, cruet Mr. and Mrs. England, case of spoons Mr. J. W. Scott, eiderdown - Miss E. Grey, table centre Miss A. Wallingt m, photo frames Miss E. Atkinson, Photo frames Mr. W. Barnes and Miss B. Wallington, damask table- cloth Mr. and Mrs. Yongs, Wordsworth's poems Mrs. Winks, d'oyleys Mrs. Lowe, ornaments Mr. and Mrs. Burns, ornaments Mrs. Heath, fruit dish Mr. and Mrs. Dale, trinket set Mr. John Weir, copper kettle</p>
